0..74 Comment "// A function written as `fun (q) { e }` acts on a path through `Path.ap`."
75..77 Comment "//"
78..152 Comment "// Whiskering composes each path of a path of paths with a fixed path. The"
153..225 Comment "// function that does it is short, and a stated type for it only repeats"
226..245 Comment "// the path\'s type."
246..248 Comment "//"
249..321 Comment "// The binder takes the type of the path\'s points. Where no path type is"
322..388 Comment "// stated, `Path.ap` reads its own off the path type the body has."
389..391 Comment "//"
392..460 Comment "// - see: #3773 — a lambda as `Path.ap`\'s function, refused before"
461..534 Comment "// - see: #3829 — a lambda where no path type is stated, refused before"
535..605 Comment "// - see: #3919 — a lambda stating its binder\'s type, refused before"
